## Kyte–Doolittle hydropathy — published (not a bundled file)

The 20 hydropathy values painted onto the ``phobic`` channel of a surface-topology map. Kept as a
literal in `src/tcren/surface.py` (`KYTE_DOOLITTLE`) rather than a CSV: twenty numbers that have not
changed since 1982.

- Origin: Kyte J, Doolittle RF. *A simple method for displaying the hydropathic character of a
  protein.* J Mol Biol. 1982;157(1):105–132. Table 1, the "hydropathy index" column.
- Independent check: r = +0.84 (n = 20) against the hydrophobicity axis
  `Potential.hydrophobicity_fit()` recovers from `MJ1996_contact_energies.csv` — the alternative
  scale `surface_map(..., scale="mj")` selects. Two unrelated derivations of the same axis, so a
  transcription slip would break the agreement rather than hide in it.
- Loader: `tcren.surface.KYTE_DOOLITTLE`.

## `holdout_model.npz` and `holdout_manifest.csv.gz` — derived frozen model

The bundled model retains the original frozen numerical parameters. The manifest names its
training population; the original metadata records 6,429 positive and 1,155 negative complete
training observations over 31 epitopes. Shared nonlinear preprocessing was trained on both
classes; binder moments and confidence moments use label-selected positives. The tier-1
one-class readouts therefore do not imply label-free or negative-independent training.

- Loader: `tcren.score.holdout_model()`; manifest: `tcren.score.holdout_manifest()`.
- Historical recipe: `tcren features -s <manifest structures> -o hold.tsv`, then
  `tcren fit-holdout --features hold.tsv --manifest src/tcren/data/holdout_manifest.csv.gz -o refit.npz`.
  Always write a separate output: evaluation never overwrites the shipped frozen fit.
- Metadata-only migration, 2026-10-14: corrected reduced spring units, finite-grid rupture scope,
  truncated Betti difference and approximate contact-loss labels. `training_catalogue_digest`
  retains the original fitted catalogue; `catalogue_digest` identifies the corrected interface.
  `tests/assets/score/frozen-metadata-migration.json` records both digests, old/new bundle hashes,
  and the SHA-256 of all five unchanged numeric arrays. No refitting occurred.
- Semantic migration: class-II chain-keyed literature descriptors, constrained shear direction,
  Potts chain-keyed sites/sampling, and corrected structure-selection/annotation/frame boundaries
  can change future descriptor outputs. Array identity establishes parameter preservation only;
  it does not certify equivalence of corrected features, a fresh refit, or scientific results.
  Matched fresh reproduction owns compatibility assessment before publication or release.
- Spring units use the default multiplicity/distance² with distances in Å: reduced stiffness
  Å^-2, force Å^-1, work dimensionless, all with an unspecified energy scale. No SI calibration
  was inferred. Unit/count spring weighting has a different arbitrary scale, documented by the API.

