## Experimental chemical core — derived resource, 20 October 2026

`chemical-core-count-1` is a separately generated empirical reference dependency,
not a bundled force field or raw experimental energy measurement. Its inputs are
existing native class-I CDR:peptide contact observations and the existing curated
antibody peptide-target contact population, exported as physical heavy-atom pairs
at 5 Å. Preserve the original input source/curation provenance and membership
accounting privately where access requires it; public documentation does not
release those structures, identifiers or contact tables.

Regenerate into a new output with neutral file placeholders:
`tcren contact-chemical-core-fit --native observations.parquet --external curated.parquet -o chemical-core.json -t 0`.
Pin exact input hashes, producer version, physical source counts and membership
counts with the resulting immutable resource; record its hash in each consuming
scoring run. No numerical resource or hash is asserted by this recipe alone.

The potential-specific 19-type map separates carbonyl sites, methionine/cysteine
sulfur and unknown-state histidine ring nitrogen without changing the general
contact classifier. Actual contact counts determine symmetric unordered
chemical enrichment; role-specific residue-conditional endpoint compositions
supply the partition. Unseen W=1 is a neutral core completion, while unmapped or
zero-conditional-support queries explicitly abstain. Mapping, reference measure,
completion and mean-per-edge unit addition are versioned together. Counts are
correlated observations and the pooled mixture can be antibody dominated.

All estimation and scoring definitions belong to the library CLI. No assay
labels, fitted combination/source weights, radial/angular or site fit enters
this experimental recipe. Values are dimensionless composition log ratios, not
physical binding free energies or independent likelihoods; neither transfer
accuracy nor a default-model change follows from the estimator. Full equations,
normalization and support policies: docs/contact-penalties.rst; frozen design:
docs/CHEMICAL_CORE_SPEC.md. Original TCRen and existing candidate resources are retained.


## Frozen task-matched ranking references — 22 October 2026

The bundled epitope-ranking and screen references are derived empirical scale
resources, not experimental energy measurements or coefficient-free models.
Means and scales come from a held-out pool of 729 models over 14 off-panel
epitopes. Query cohorts and labels do not estimate these moments at scoring time.
The screen signs are fixed a priori; saved training-pool ROC values check those
signs and are label-dependent diagnostics, not independently estimated directions.
The TCR confidence weight of 0.8 is an explicit design choice informed by recorded
evaluation, not a prospectively validated learned parameter. Epitope weight 0.5
retains the existing equal-weight readout. Applicability cuts and their reference
populations are stored with the resources; flags report by default.

Private input lineage and the exact producer revision are retained in the
benchmark's `bench/scripts/make_screen_references.py` and its release records.
No rerun or new estimation is authorized by this registry. Reproduction requires
the source-verified held-out training inputs and exclusion ledger, not query data.
The resources remain frozen during release verification. SHA-256 identities:
